#     - 1.0.0 (10/30/2026) [dendogg + Anthropic - Claude Opus 5.5] — First
#       release, with the repository's first commit: text files keep LF line
#       endings in the repository and the working copy, and the models,
#       engine, sounds and images are stored as binary.
#
# ✒ Description:
#     How Git treats the project's files. Every text file is written with LF
#     endings, and this keeps them that way on every machine, whatever the
#     local core.autocrlf setting, so a checkout never rewrites the page's
#     sources with CRLF.
#
# ✒ Key Features:
#     - text=auto eol=lf: text files are normalised to LF and checked out as
#       LF, on Windows as elsewhere.
#     - The engine's WebAssembly, the .glb and .blend models, the sounds and
#       the images are marked binary: never converted, never diffed as text.
#     - The vendored engine script keeps its bytes as shipped (-text).
#
# ✒ Other Important Information:
#     - Dependencies: Git.
#     - Compatible platforms: any Git client.
#     - After changing a rule here, `git add --renormalize .` applies it to
#       files already tracked.
#
# ---------

* text=auto eol=lf

*.wasm binary
*.glb binary
*.blend binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.mp3 binary

engine/stockfish-19-lite-single.js -text
